                <pb facs="0287" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg205"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Campbell</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 20.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 17, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 26, of September 26, has
                    been received. It is gratifying to hear of the friendship of Sweden and Norway
                    for this government, as expressed by Count Manderstròm at your last
                    interview.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James H. Campbell,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Stockholm.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
